37\nJun    260\nJul    297\nAug    309\nSep    308\nOct    387\nNov    374\nDec    421\nName: count, dtype: int64\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 900x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1200x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":215},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*App updates increase every year, from just 1 app in 2010 to 1,826 in 2017 and 6,934 in 2018. The monthly line shows updates staying low for years and then rising sharply in 2018. Most apps were updated recently because the data was collected in August 2018. This is also why July looks like the busiest month (2,653 apps updated in July 2018 alone), so July is not a real seasonal peak. Looking only at 2010 to 2017, updates slowly rise in the second half of the year, with October to December (374 to 421 apps a month) higher than January to May (185 to 237). This suggests developers update more toward the end of the year, possibly before the holiday season. The dataset only has the latest update date for each app, so this pattern is a rough sign and not a confirmed trend.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**3. How does the average rating of apps change with the number of installs? Create a binned analysis.**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"rating_by_installs = df.groupby(\"Install_Bin\", observed=True)[\"Rating\"].agg([\"mean\", \"count\"]).round(2)\nprint(rating_by_installs)\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 5))\nsns.barplot(x=rating_by_installs.index, y=rating_by_installs[\"mean\"])\nplt.xlabel(\"Install Range\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Average Rating\")\nplt.title(\"Average Rating by Install Range\")\nplt.ylim(3.5, 4.5)\nplt.tight_layout()\nsavefig(\"a3_rating_by_install_range.png\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-19T09:53:42.93054Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-19T09:53:42.931015Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-19T09:53:43.764394Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-19T09:53:42.930972Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-19T09:53:43.762903Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"             mean  count\nInstall_Bin             \n0-1K         4.20   1337\n1K-10K       4.03   1415\n10K-100K     4.09   1572\n100K-1M      4.21   2002\n1M-10M       4.29   1815\n10M-100M     4.38    641\n100M+        4.31    110\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":216},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*Average rating goes up as apps get more installs. It is lowest for apps with 1K to 10K installs (4.03) and highest for 10M to 100M installs (4.38). Apps with 100M+ installs stay high at 4.31. Apps with under 1K installs also show a high 4.20, because a few reviews from friends or early users can easily give them a good score. Overall, popular apps usually have better ratings, but the change is small (about 0.35 points), so ratings depend on more than installs.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**4. Perform sentiment analysis on app reviews (if review text is available) to determine the common themes in high and low-rated apps.**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"from textblob import TextBlob\n\n# use the cleaned reviews and add each app's rating\nreviews_rated = reviews.copy()\nreviews_rated[\"App_Rating\"] = reviews_rated[\"App\"].map(app_level.set_index(\"App\")[\"Rating\"])\nreviews_rated = reviews_rated.dropna(subset=[\"App_Rating\"])\n\n# NLP: score each review text with TextBlob\nreviews_rated[\"My_Polarity\"] = reviews_rated[\"Translated_Review\"].apply(lambda t: TextBlob(str(t)).sentiment.polarity)\nreviews_rated[\"My_Sentiment\"] = np.where(reviews_rated[\"My_Polarity\"] > 0, \"Positive\",\n                                np.where(reviews_rated[\"My_Polarity\"] < 0, \"Negative\", \"Neutral\"))\n\nprint(\"TextBlob matches dataset labels (%):\",\n      round((reviews_rated[\"My_Sentiment\"] == reviews_rated[\"Sentiment\"]).mean() * 100, 1))\n\nhigh = reviews_rated[reviews_rated[\"App_Rating\"] >= 4.5]\nlow = reviews_rated[reviews_rated[\"App_Rating\"] < 4.0]\n\nprint(\"High rated apps:\", high[\"App\"].nunique(), \"apps,\", len(high), \"reviews\")\nprint(\"Low rated apps:\", low[\"App\"].nunique(), \"apps,\", len(low), \"reviews\")\nprint(\"Average polarity, high rated:\", round(high[\"My_Polarity\"].mean(), 3))\nprint(\"Average polarity, low rated:\", round(low[\"My_Polarity\"].mean(), 3))\n\n# sentiment share in each group\nsentiment = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"High Rated (4.5+)\": high[\"My_Sentiment\"].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100,\n    \"Low Rated (below 4.0)\": low[\"My_Sentiment\"].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100\n}).round(1)\nprint(sentiment)\n\nsentiment.plot(kind=\"bar\", figsize=(9, 5))\nplt.xlabel(\"Sentiment\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Percent of Reviews\")\nplt.title(\"Review Sentiment: High vs Low Rated Apps\")\nplt.xticks(rotation=0)\nplt.tight_layout()\nsavefig(\"a4_sentiment_comparison.png\")\n\n# group review words into themes\nthemes = {\n    \"Ease of use\": r\"\\b(?:easy|simple|useful|helpful)\",\n    \"Bugs and crashes\": r\"\\b(?:crash|bug|freeze|error|glitch|fix|stuck)\",\n    \"Updates\": r\"\\b(?:update|version)\",\n    \"Price and payment\": r\"\\b(?:money|price|pay|paid|refund|subscription|purchase)\",\n    \"Login and account\": r\"\\b(?:login|account|password|sign)\",\n    \"Ads\": r\"\\b(?:ads|advert)\",\n    \"Speed\": r\"\\b(?:slow|fast|lag|loading)\"\n}\n\npositive_high = high[high[\"My_Sentiment\"] == \"Positive\"][\"Translated_Review\"].str.lower()\nnegative_low = low[low[\"My_Sentiment\"] == \"Negative\"][\"Translated_Review\"].str.lower()\n\ntheme_table = pd.DataFrame({\n    \"Positive reviews (high rated)\": {t: positive_high.str.contains(p).mean() * 100 for t, p in themes.items()},\n    \"Negative reviews (low rated)\": {t: negative_low.str.contains(p).mean() * 100 for t, p in themes.items()}\n}).round(1)\nprint(theme_table)\n\ntheme_table.plot(kind=\"barh\", figsize=(10, 6))\nplt.xlabel(\"Percent of Reviews Mentioning Theme\")\nplt.ylabel(\"Theme\")\nplt.title(\"Common Themes in Reviews\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nsavefig(\"a4_review_themes.png\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-19T09:53:43.768321Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-19T09:53:43.772132Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-19T09:53:59.70767Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-19T09:53:43.772077Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-19T09:53:59.706083Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"TextBlob matches dataset labels (%): 100.0\nHigh rated apps: 263 apps, 9479 reviews\nLow rated apps: 101 apps, 3358 reviews\nAverage polarity, high rated: 0.216\nAverage polarity, low rated: 0.093\n              High Rated (4.5+)  Low Rated (below 4.0)\nMy_Sentiment                                          \nPositive                   70.5                   53.2\nNegative                   19.6                   27.8\nNeutral                     9.8                   19.0\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 900x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}},{"name":"stdout","text":"                   Positive reviews (high rated)  Negative reviews (low rated)\nEase of use                                 16.5                           4.3\nBugs and crashes                             7.6                          19.1\nUpdates                                      8.3                          14.9\nPrice and payment                           10.6                           8.9\nLogin and account                            2.9                           8.0\nAds                                          4.4                           4.1\nSpeed                                        3.9                           6.9\n","output_type":"stream"},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":217},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"*I used TextBlob (an NLP library) to score the sentiment of each review text, and it matched the dataset's own labels for 100% of reviews, so the results can be trusted. High rated apps (4.5 and above) get mostly positive reviews (70.5%) with an average polarity of 0.216, while low rated apps (below 4.0) get more negative (27.8%) and neutral (19.0%) reviews with a polarity of only 0.093. In positive reviews of high rated apps, the most common theme is ease of use (16.5%), followed by price and payment (10.6%). In negative reviews of low rated apps, the top complaints are bugs and crashes (19.1%) and problems after updates (14.9%), followed by price and payment (8.9%), login issues (8.0%) and slow speed (6.9%). Fixing bugs and testing updates well can help improve an app's rating.*","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**5. What is the relationship between app genre and user ratings? Are certain genres consistently rated higher or lower?**","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# mean and median rating for each genre\ngenre_rating = df.groupby(\"Genres\")[\"Rating\"].agg([\"mean\", \"median\", \"std\", \"count\"]).round(2)\nprint(\"Total genres:\", len(genre_rating))\n\n# keep genres with 30 or more rated apps so the averages are reliable\ngenre_rating = genre_rating[genre_rating[\"count\"] >= 30].sort_values(\"mean\", ascending=False)\nprint(\"Genres with 30 or more rated apps:\", len(genre_rating))\nprint(genre_rating)\n\ntop10 = genre_rating.head(10)\nbottom10 = genre_rating.tail(10)\n\nfig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 6))\n\naxes[0].barh(top10.index[::-1], top10[\"mean\"][::-1])\naxes[0].set_title(\"Top 10 Highest Rated Genres\")\naxes[0].set_xlabel(\"Average Rating\")\naxes[0].set_xlim(3.5, 4.6)\n\naxes[1].barh(bottom10.index[::-1], bottom10[\"mean\"][::-1])\naxes[1].set_tit